the Chimera in Greek mythology the  Chimera is a monster with the body and  head of a lion a snake for a tail and a  fire-breathing goat head protruding from  its back the appearance of the Chimera  can vary there are versions where it has  the hind legs of a goat with wings and  even the head of a dragon sibling to the  Hydra and servers much like many of the  other monsters in Greek mythology the  Chimera is the daughter of Typhon and  echidna the mere sight of the Chimera  was considered a bad omen as the monster  would often appear before natural  disasters such as violent storms and  volcanic eruptions the Chimera took  residence in Licio and for many years  terrorized the neighboring towns and  villages in fear for his kingdom king  low with us turned to bella la throne  the son of Poseidon to aid him and  destroying the Beast once he accepted  the cause of his king Bella Lefranc  consulted with the soothsayer Politis  who advised him to seek help from the  winged horse Pegasus in order to do this  bola front would have to spend the night  in the temple of Minerva as he slept  Minerva came to him and gave him a  golden bridle when he awoke Minerva took  him to Pegasus and at the sight of the  golden bridle the steed came willingly  to aid him bellow the front mounted  Pegasus and they took to the skies and  searched for the Chimera flying above  the Chimera bell Allah from was able to  rain down arrows upon the creature his  efforts were in vain as the Chimera was  able to melt his arrowheads before they  made any contact the Chimera began to  overpower bell Olaf run and he steed  with the sheer power of its fiery breath  Bellerophon had the idea of attaching a  lump of lead to the point of his spear  and thrusting it in between the jaws of  the Chimera  the creatures fiery breath melted the  lead which trickled down its throat burn  in its insights instantly killing the  Beast many believe that the Chimera  is a symbol of the volcano located in  Licio the surrounding area was known for  its constant burning fires hence the  name mount chimera if you've enjoyed  this video then please consider leaving  a thumbs up as it helps promote the  video and allows the channel to grow if  there's anything you'd like to discuss  or have any ideas for future videos then  please let me know in the comment  section as always I've been your host  mythology and folklore explain
 

